_coverage":null,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":-0.0478902896633642,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":82.0,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.07742381589790978,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":92.2,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.0029736780759730963,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":96.3,"_gate_piotroski":8,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":88.9,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.02873087567679633,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":28.5,"_gate_rev_durability":0.11749576909462123,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":83.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02390022383631903,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":37.7,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.001149668592699049,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":51.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03181609597272906,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":47.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00493,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"TransUnion operates as a global consumer credit reporting agency that provides risk and information solutions. The company operates in two segments, U.S. Markets and International. The U.S. Markets segment provides credit reporting, credit marketing, analytics and consulting, identity verification, and authentication and debt recovery solutions for financial services industry; and onboarding and transaction processing products, scoring and analytic products, marketing solutions, fraud and identity management solutions, and customer retention solutions, as well select market-specific solutions for insurance, technology, retail and e-commerce, telecommunications, media, tenant and employment screening, collections, and public sectors. It also offers credit reports, scores, and freezes credit monitoring, identity protection and resolution, and financial management for consumers, as well as helps businesses respond to data breach events through its own websites, as well as channels. The International segment offers credit reports, analytics, technology solutions, and other value-added risk management services; consumer services, which helps consumers to manage their personal finances; credit bureaus; and consumer and business credit reporting, insurance and auto information solutions, and commercial credit information services. This segment serves customers in financial services, retail credit, insurance, automotive, collections, public sector, and communications industries through direct and indirect channels. The company was formerly known as TransUnion Holding Company, Inc. and changed its name to TransUnion in March 2015. TransUnion was founded in 1968 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher A. Cartwright | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $4.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $339K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $49K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["TransUnion is a large-cap financial services business with a $15.5B market cap on $4.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $662M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.17\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Price sits 26% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.26128280152168165},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (47% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Financial Services peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"TransUnion (NYSE:TRU) Insider Sells $77,740.00 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/transunion-nysetru-insider-sells-77740-00-in-stock.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793961732.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.9,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"TransUnion (TRU) Jumped, What Is Behind The Latest Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-tru/transunion/news/transunion-tru-jumped-what-is-behind-the-latest-attention","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793878968.388,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.944,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"TRU (NYSE:TRU) Earnings Beat and Dividend Increase Signal Credit Bureau Strength","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/financial/tru-nysetru-earnings-beat-and-dividend-increase-signal-credit-bureau-strength","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793816460.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.683,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"TransUnion Appoints David Gilbert as Interim Chief Financial Officer","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/transunion-appoints-david-gilbert-inte